[P_04_Penthouse_Gnome_Lambert]
Speech_-001L=(null)
Speech_0049L=FISHER - Lambert... he doesn't want to cooperate. What do I do?
Speech_0050L=LAMBERT - I don't know... better check out the next room.
Speech_0051L=LAMBERT - I don't know... I think you're going to need to figure out how to operate that thing on your own.
Speech_-001L=(null)
Speech_0037L=LAMBERT - Fisher... what are you doing?
Speech_0038L=FISHER - I've seen these things before... this is a finite state machine.
Speech_0039L=LAMBERT - It is?
Speech_0040L=FISHER - Yeah. Looks like Dvorak is just the encoded innards of a fifty year old scrap heap.
Speech_0041L=GRIMSDOTTIR - No wonder I couldn't hack into it.
Speech_0042L=FISHER - It doesn't even speak the same language. I'm going to try and reinitialize the machine and retrieve an output stack for analysis. 
Speech_0043L=GRIMSDOTTIR - Gotcha.
Speech_-001L=(null)
Speech_0044L=FISHER - Alright, I've got the stack.
Speech_0045L=GRIMSDOTTIR - Fisher... judging by what we just saw, I think that's an infinite state machine... not a finite state machine.
Speech_0046L=FISHER - What's the difference?
Speech_0047L=GRIMSDOTTIR - This one is self-referential. Each output stack is a logical  instruction set that tells the machine to recurse itself and derive a more accurate set of instructions for the execution cycle.
Speech_0048L=FISHER - Fascinating. Can I go now?
Speech_-001L=(null)
Speech_0024L=FISHER - Lambert... what the hell is this thing?
Speech_0025L=LAMBERT - I have no idea Fisher... talk to the old man... maybe he knows something.
Speech_-001L=(null)
Speech_0026L=FISHER - Lambert... what the hell is this thing?
Speech_0027L=LAMBERT - I don't know Fisher...but I bet that old man would have helped us if...
Speech_0028L=FISHER - Well too late... now what do we do?
Speech_0029L=LAMBERT - Grim?
Speech_0030L=GRIMSDOTTIR - It looks like a finite state machine... weird academic sixties era university basement crap.
Speech_0031L=FISHER - What should I do?
Speech_0032L=GRIMSDOTTIR - You'll need to retrieve an output stack. Restart the machine, then hit the switch on each tower in sequence when the tube heats up. Once you're done, you'll need to recover the output stack.
Speech_-001L=(null)
Speech_0052L=LAMBERT - Grim?
Speech_0053L=GRIMSDOTTIR - It looks like a finite state machine... weird academic sixties era university basement crap.
Speech_0054L=FISHER - What should I do?
Speech_0055L=GRIMSDOTTIR - You'll need to retrieve and output stack. Restart the machine, then hit the switch on each tower in sequence when the tube heats up. Once you're done, you'll need to recover the output stack.
Speech_-001L=(null)
Speech_0033L=GRIMSDOTTIR - It looks like the tubes will overheat and reset if you don't initialize the tower fast enough. You'll need to restart the whole sequence over again.
Speech_-001L=(null)
Speech_0034L=GRIMSDOTTIR - No good, you'll have to try again.
Speech_-001L=(null)
Speech_0035L=GRIMSDOTTIR - You took too long. You need to initialize each tower before the main tube overheats.
Speech_-001L=(null)
Speech_0036L=GRIMSDOTTIR - Too slow. Restart the machine again.
Speech_-001L=(null)
Speech_0001L=FISHER - Lambert... something weird is happening.
Speech_0002L=LAMBERT - I'll say.
Speech_0003L=FISHER - What do I do?
Speech_0004L=LAMBERT - The old man seems harmless. Indulge him. See if he knows anything.
Speech_-001L=(null)
Speech_0005L=FISHER - Jesus... I think I just figured out why you couldn't hack in here Grim...
Speech_0006L=GRIMSDOTTIR - Uh... yeah... no kidding
Speech_0007L=FISHER - What the hell do I do now?
Speech_0008L=GRIMSDOTTIR - Uh... hold on while I find a slide rule...
Speech_0009L=LAMBERT - See what the old man knows, Fisher.
Speech_-001L=(null)
Speech_0010L=FISHER - Right. Grim...did you get that?
Speech_0011L=GRIMSDOTTIR - My god... It's an infinite state machine.
Speech_0014L=FISHER - Fine. What do I do?
Speech_0015L=GRIMSDOTTIR - ... if Zherkezhi is using this...
Speech_0016L=FISHER - Grim.
Speech_0017L=GRIMSDOTTIR - Sorry. Uh. Sam, we're going to need to a copy of Dvorak's outputs so we can work out the algorithm it's built on.
Speech_0018L=FISHER - How do I get its output?
Speech_0019L=GRIMSDOTTIR - It runs on punch cards.
Speech_0020L=FISHER - Punch cards?
Speech_0021L=GRIMSDOTTIR - You'll need to restart the sequence and initialize each tower in the right order and then retrieve the output stack.
Speech_0022L=FISHER - How do I know the right sequence?
Speech_0023L=GRIMSDOTTIR - You'll need to hit the switches in order as the tubes start to heat up. Ask the old man for help.

